search the first start &gt;= start, check the predecessor's end + gap &lt;= start and end + gap

27
00:02:32.182 --> 00:02:38.193
&lt;= the successor's start, and splice the new booking in. For cancel, look up the start, binary search

28
00:02:38.193 --> 00:02:42.487
it and splice it out. For next, return the first start &gt;= time.

29
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:50.268
Non-overlapping intervals form a total order, so a new booking has exactly one predecessor and one successor,

30
00:02:50.268 --> 00:02:51.623
and no farther booking can

31
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:59.368
be closer. Binary search finds that position in O(log n). The array splice that keeps the order shifts

